{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And the meaning of \"they shall tremble like a bird\"</b> — that a bird trembles at the sound of a lion, but I will fly like a bird and like a dove — the opposite of what He said: \"a silly dove without heart.\"" "<b>And I will settle them in their houses</b> — the meaning is: I will restore their captives, only they do not follow HaShem, for they surround Me with falsehood and deceit, not in truth. Likewise Judah, who would say: \"for God is with [us],\" on the pattern of \"for if the money is complete\" — because he supposed, on account of the kings being of the house of David, that it is the kingdom of HaShem."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :register {:flags {1 ["God"]}}, :notes {1 "The phrase כי רד עם אל (Hosea 11:12 in the Hebrew verse numbering) is cryptic; translated hyper-literally. Ibn Ezra's comparison to כי אם תם הסכר (Proverbs?) is textually uncertain; rendered as 'for if the money is complete' following the consonantal text."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:59.244123723Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}